.TH TDE-SYSTEMD-MANAGER 1 "November 2026" "tde-systemd 1.0.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde-systemd-manager \- manage systemd services and system settings in TDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde-systemd-manager
[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-unit\fR \fIunit\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR]]
[\fIgeneric TDE and Qt options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde-systemd-manager
is a graphical front end to
.BR systemd (1)
for the Trinity Desktop Environment. It shows the state of the system and
lists the units of the system manager and of the user's service manager.
Units can be started, stopped, restarted, reloaded, enabled, disabled,
masked and unmasked; their status, unit file, properties, dependencies and
log are shown. A timer overview shows when each timer last ran and when it
runs next.
.PP
If the corresponding systemd services are installed, additional pages
change the date, time, time zone and network time synchronization
(\fBsystemd-timedated\fR), the hostname and machine information
(\fBsystemd-hostnamed\fR), and the system locale and keyboard layout
(\fBsystemd-localed\fR). These optional pages can be hidden in the
\fISettings\fR menu.
.PP
Reading information never requires special rights. Changes to the system
are carried out by
.BR tde-systemd-helper (8)
after authorization through
.BR polkit (8);
a polkit authentication agent such as \fBpolkit-agent-tde\fR must be
running in the session. Operations on user units run directly with the
user's rights.
.PP
The same functionality is available as the TDE Control Center module
\fBSystemd Services\fR (\fBtdecmshell tdesystemd\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " name"
Show the given page first. \fIname\fR is one of \fBoverview\fR,
\fBservices\fR, \fBtimers\fR, \fBdatetime\fR, \fBhostname\fR or
\fBlocale\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-unit " unit"
Show the services page and select \fIunit\fR, for example
\fBsshd.service\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-user
Look up the unit given with \fB\-\-unit\fR in the user's service manager
instead of the system manager.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a summary of the options. \fB\-\-help\-all\fR also lists the generic
TDE and Qt options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tde-systemdrc
Settings, e.g. which optional pages are shown (group \fB[Pages]\fR, keys
\fBShowDateTime\fR, \fBShowHostname\fR and \fBShowLocale\fR).
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.policy
The polkit actions used for system changes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tde-systemd-manager \-\-unit cups.service
Open the manager with the CUPS service selected.
.TP
.B tde-systemd-manager \-\-page timers
Show the timer overview.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tde-journal-viewer (1),
